The desk merged reports with similar subjects. To route a new report, look up the tenant’s locale and booking form, then check which channel received the date. Intake tags describe the browser’s initial guess.

## Where to file a report

[Shared parser, issue 1](https://github.com/correasebastian/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1). The shared parser reads a day-first date as month first. Report R-41200 describes an April 7 reminder sent on July 4.

[Booking-v3 hint, issue 2](https://github.com/correasebastian/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2). The booking-v3 form shows MM/DD/YYYY to day-first tenants and interprets the entry in local order. Report R-41230 came through that form and received a parser tag at intake.

## Report counts

The table counts distinct report IDs merged into ticket 4471. Its ticket column describes the original desk export. Use the two linked issues for follow-up. The one-day-move notes remain in their tenant-assigned group pending investigation.

